# No autopilot in agent path (0.5+)

The LLM is the **only planner**. Python must not auto-dispatch tools during `run_agent`.

## Forbidden in agent loop

- Auto `apply_plan` / `diagnose_failure` / `slice` before or instead of LLM steps
- `NEXT_ACTION` imperative bootstrap blocks
- Default needles (`error_text="License"`) when observation is missing
- `argus_apply_plan` without explicit `steps=` from the model

## Allowed

- `bootstrap_evidence` — lightweight observations + `hints.suggested_tools`
- `recovery_hints_from_trace` — text hints only, no `dispatch_tool`
- Deterministic **backends** (`diagnose_failure`, `gate_scan`) when LLM calls the tool
- `ARGUS_FAST_PATH=1` or `argus debug fast-path` for regression only
- `_evaluate_tasks` truth model

## Tool contract

Tools return: `observations`, `evidence`, optional `hints`, `verify`. Never execute the next tool on behalf of the model.
